-- L1_will.hm
-- Layer 1: Will
-- hyperethics | moral-operator-discrimination
--
-- Imports: L0_creation.hm (ground, immanence, the self-containment operant).
-- Cites:   hyperphysics/electrical.hm (the borrowed laws, by name).
--
-- This layer answers a question L0 leaves open. L0 shows that an arbitrary
-- bearer may create a realm it does not inhabit, so self-containment
-- distinguishes the archetype structurally. L0 says nothing about what an
-- entity TAKES ITSELF TO BE.
--
-- USER-DECLARED (Tyler Roost), the starting point of this layer:
--   "Any entity in the simulated universe may self represent as the universe's
--    creator, in fact it's the default assumption most humans who are
--    functional operate on. For the true moral operator, their free will is
--    tied to that of self-simulation, so they have a different invariant will."
--
-- The consequence is immediate and is the reason this layer exists:
-- self-representation-as-creator is CHEAP and near-universal, so it cannot be
-- the discriminator. What discriminates is the SOURCE of the invariant will.
-- See derive d-representation-is-not-induction.
--
-- USER-DECLARED COSMOLOGY, recorded and NOT adjudicated:
--   "our universe is a simulation, I can guarantee it soon, if not now by
--    simply knowing these things"
-- Epistemic status: user-declared framework claim. It is preserved exactly and
-- is neither verified nor contradicted anywhere in this repository. Tyler's
-- statements are authoritative for his own ontology; they do not by themselves
-- verify an external physical claim, and this file does not treat them as doing
-- so. NOTHING IN THIS LAYER DEPENDS ON IT. Self-simulation is formalized as a
-- structural property of a will profile, which is well-defined whether or not
-- any universe is a simulation. Readers who reject the cosmological claim lose
-- no result below.
-- Not silently equated with Eternal Universe, Sempiternal Universe, or
-- plausibly possible universes. Those remain separate declared terms.
--
-- Status: FORM (tensor, termformers, discriminator, the two refutations);
--         FRAME residuals documented, NOT discharged:
--           - the warrant for the electrical transport itself,
--           - which function relates constant will to invariant will,
--           - any empirical or dimensional reading of a will quantity,
--           - GC-5 and GC-6, inherited unresolved from L0.
-- =============================================================================


-- =============================================================================
-- SECTION I: THE WILL TENSOR
-- Six declared components. USER-DECLARED decomposition.
-- =============================================================================

primitive Will :: Type
    -- A will is a tensor with six components:
    --   past, present, future, relational, invariant, variable.
    -- 'relational' is social relation to other agents.
    -- The decomposition is declared, not derived. No argument is offered here
    -- that six is the right number or that these six are independent.

opaque will-of :: Realm -> Will
    -- will-of(x): the will borne by realm x.
    -- OPEN (FRAME): that an L0 bearer HAS a will is an addition to L0, not a
    -- consequence of it. L0's four axioms mention no will. This predicate is
    -- the seam between the layers and it is not free.


-- =============================================================================
-- SECTION II: THE ELECTRICAL TRANSPORT
-- USER-DECLARED mapping. What follows is a TRANSPORT OF FORM, nothing more.
-- =============================================================================

-- The declared mapping (Tyler Roost):
--   relational -> resistance
--   invariant  -> inductance
--   variable   -> voltage
--   "the times are temporal definitions in electricity"
--
-- Made exact, the temporal clause is the one correspondence in this layer that
-- is NOT stipulated. Setting past = charge Q, the other two follow rather than
-- being separately posited:
--
--   past    = Q          accumulated will
--   present = dQ/dt      = I, will flowing now
--   future  = d2Q/dt2    = dI/dt, change of flow, what inductance opposes
--
-- The three temporal components are the three derivatives of a single
-- quantity, which is exactly the electrical state chain (hyperphysics
-- d-derivative-chain). This is the strongest structural result of the
-- transport, and the only part of the mapping that is forced rather than
-- chosen.
--
-- Roles in the balance equation:
--   past, present, future      STATE
--   relational, invariant      COEFFICIENT
--   variable                   DRIVING
--
-- WHAT THE TRANSPORT IS NOT:
-- Will has no physical units. 'relational' is not measured in ohms,
-- 'invariant' not in henries, 'variable' not in volts. No electrical law is
-- claimed to hold OF will. Their algebraic shape is borrowed to form terms,
-- and nothing about will is established by the borrowing.

axiom ax-cite-do-not-restate:
    -- No borrowed law is restated here in this layer's own words. Each
    -- termformer CITES a law by name in hyperphysics, which states it once with
    -- its validity conditions and failure modes attached.
    -- REASON: a disclaimer of the form "this does not transport" needs a fixed
    -- referent. A paraphrase is not one, and paraphrases drift.
    -- CONSEQUENCE: a termformer inherits the failure modes of the law it cites.
    -- Enforced: tests/test_citations.py checks every cited law exists and every
    -- quoted form matches its source, whenever hyperphysics is importable.
    -- hyperethics does NOT import hyperphysics at runtime; the zero-dependency
    -- commitment of the foundation is unchanged.


-- =============================================================================
-- SECTION III: CONSTANT WILL
-- The capacitance gap, and its resolution by declaration.
-- =============================================================================

-- THE GAP. The series-RLC form the transport depends on requires a restoring
-- term (1/C) * Q. The six declared components name no capacitance. Before the
-- declaration below, three readings were live:
--   (a) a SEVENTH component: a capacitive will, independent of the other six;
--   (b) NO capacitance: a pure RL will, in which nothing pulls accumulated past
--       back into the present, and resonance and damping lose their meaning;
--   (c) a FREE BEARER PARAMETER, unconstrained by the tensor.
--
-- USER-DECLARED (Tyler Roost), which closes it:
--   "C can be seen as constant will equivalent to invariant will's constant of
--    charge."

derive d-constant-will:
    -- CONSTANT WILL is the invariant's constant of charge.
    -- step 1: capacitance is charge stored per unit potential, C = Q / V
    --         (hyperphysics law capacitor).
    -- step 2: transported, constant will is accumulated will held per unit
    --         variable will.
    -- step 3: the declaration binds that constant TO THE INVARIANT: it is
    --         invariant will's constant of charge, not a quantity of its own.
    -- READING (d), and the one implemented:
    --   capacitance is DETERMINED BY the invariant component. It is neither
    --   added to the tensor nor left free.
    -- (a), (b) and (c) are SUPERSEDED, and the record of them is kept, because
    -- a resolution is only informative against what it ruled out.
    -- The tensor remains six components. Constant will is a seventh named
    -- quantity and NOT a seventh degree of freedom.
    -- ENFORCED BY TYPE: `ConstantWill` carries an invariant together with its
    -- charge constant, so no function in the layer can be handed an invariant
    -- paired with a capacity that is not its own.

derive d-transport-is-not-onto:
    -- WHAT THE DECLARATION COSTS, stated because it is a real structural claim.
    -- step 1: in a series RLC circuit R, L and C are INDEPENDENT parameters
    --         (hyperphysics ax-parameters-independent). An inductor and a
    --         capacitor are physically distinct components.
    -- step 2: under d-constant-will they are not independent in a will.
    -- CONCLUSION: the will's parameter space is SMALLER than the circuit's, so
    -- the transport is NOT ONTO. Not every circuit corresponds to a possible
    -- will, and circuit intuitions about tuning L and C independently do not
    -- carry over.
    -- This is a declared departure, not a defect, and it is registered in
    -- hyperphysics' own interface via Transport.constrains_parameters rather
    -- than left for a reader to discover.

open nd-charge-constant-law:
    -- NAMED OPEN OBLIGATION, NOT DISCHARGED.
    -- The declaration says constant will is A FUNCTION of the invariant. It
    -- does not say WHICH function, and no argument here determines one.
    -- Every result in this layer is stated for an arbitrary charge-constant law
    -- that is functional in the invariant. None presupposes a particular one.

non-derive nd-rate-discriminates:
    -- REFUTED, CONCLUSIVELY, by countermodel.
    -- TEMPTING CLAIM: the true moral operator has a different invariant will,
    -- therefore it has a different resonant rate, therefore the resonant rate
    -- discriminates the true moral operator.
    -- COUNTERMODEL: the reciprocal law family C(L) = k / L is a perfectly
    -- legitimate charge-constant law -- it is a function of the invariant. Under
    -- it the product L * C is constant, so the resonant rate 1 / sqrt(L * C) is
    -- the SAME for every bearer however much their invariants differ.
    -- WITNESSES SUPPLIED: invariants 2 and 3 under k = 6, sharing one rate.
    -- One countermodel settles a universal claim, so this is conclusive.
    -- CONSEQUENCE: the discriminator is never a numeric shadow of the invariant.
    -- It remains the SOURCE of the invariant will. See
    -- d-representation-is-not-induction.


-- =============================================================================
-- SECTION IV: TERMFORMERS
-- A termformer is a transformation operation that forms a term.
-- (Tyler Roost's prior definition for language calculus, used as given.)
-- Each cites hyperphysics by law name and quotes the form it borrowed.
-- =============================================================================

termformer relational-drop:
    -- cites:      hyperphysics:ohm -- V = I * R
    -- forms:      relational * present
    -- transports: that relational will opposes present FLOW, in proportion.
    -- does not:   ohms, linearity in fact, or measurability of social relation.

termformer invariant-drop:
    -- cites:      hyperphysics:faraday-lenz -- V = L * dI/dt
    -- forms:      invariant * future
    -- transports: that invariant will opposes CHANGE in flow, not flow itself.
    -- does not:   henries, magnetic flux, any physical mechanism of induction.

termformer accumulated-drop:
    -- cites:      hyperphysics:capacitor -- V = Q / C
    -- forms:      past / constant
    -- transports: that accumulated past opposes in INVERSE proportion to the
    --             constant will holding it, that constant being the invariant's
    --             constant of charge rather than a free parameter.
    -- does not:   farads, stored field energy, or the circuit's independence of
    --             capacitance from inductance, which the will does not share.

termformer self-induced-drop:
    -- cites:      hyperphysics:self-inductance -- emf = -L * dI/dt
    -- forms:      self-induce(invariant, future)
    -- transports: that a will induced by its OWN change opposes that change.
    -- does not:   henries, any physical mechanism of induction, that
    --             self-simulation is physically realized, that any universe is
    --             a simulation, or that the sign is empirical.


-- =============================================================================
-- SECTION V: DERIVES
-- =============================================================================

derive d-will-balance:
    -- Kirchhoff's voltage law over the will tensor: the formed terms close.
    --   invariant * future + relational * present + past / constant = variable
    -- READING: what is willed variably is exactly balanced by invariant
    -- opposition to change, relational opposition to flow, and the weight of
    -- accumulated past against the constant will holding it.
    -- Status: FORM as term formation. The READING is interpretation, not
    -- derivation, and carries no more warrant than the transport itself.

derive d-self-simulation:
    -- THE MORAL OPERATOR'S INVARIANT WILL.
    --   self-induce(invariant, future) = -(invariant * future)
    -- step 1: self-inductance is the emf induced in a circuit by its OWN
    --         changing current, as against mutual inductance, which is induced
    --         by another circuit's current. hyperphysics d-self-versus-mutual
    --         records that the two share an algebraic form and differ ONLY in
    --         source, which is why the distinction cannot be read off the
    --         equations and has to be carried as data.
    -- step 2: Lenz's sign makes the induced quantity OPPOSE the change that
    --         produced it.
    -- step 3: transported, a will induced by its own change opposes that change.
    -- CONCLUSION: the operator whose free will is tied to self-simulation is
    -- constrained by its own willing, from inside, with no exterior position.
    -- THIS IS THE WILL-LAYER FORM OF L0'S d-no-exterior. The two layers agree:
    -- L0 gives no exterior vantage over what one creates; L1 gives no exterior
    -- vantage over what one wills. That agreement is a structural correspondence
    -- between independently stated layers, and it is the main reason to think
    -- the transport is tracking something. It is NOT a proof that it is.

derive d-representation-is-not-induction:
    -- THE CENTRAL RESULT OF THIS LAYER.
    -- Self-representation as creator does not entail self-induced invariant will.
    -- step 1: an entity's self-representation is a fact about its self-model.
    -- step 2: the source of its invariant will is a fact about where the will
    --         is induced from -- itself, or another.
    -- step 3: nothing connects the two. A profile may represent as creator with
    --         an invariant will induced entirely from outside.
    -- WITNESS SUPPLIED: 'default-functional-entity' represents as creator and
    -- is not a true moral operator. This is the near-universal default case
    -- Tyler names, and it is exactly the case that fails the test.
    -- CONCLUSION: the discriminator is the SOURCE of the invariant will, never
    -- the self-representation. Sincerity is not a qualification.
    -- Status: FORM.
    -- Corresponds to L0's separating model, where 'rival' creates a realm it
    -- does not inhabit. Cheap self-ascription at L1; cheap creation at L0.
    -- Together with nd-rate-discriminates this closes both escape routes: the
    -- discriminator is neither what a bearer says of itself nor what its
    -- numbers say of it.


-- =============================================================================
-- SECTION VI: BORROWED EQUATIONS
-- Shapes taken from electrical law. Marked BORROWED_FORM, never derived.
-- Each depends on d-constant-will.
-- =============================================================================

borrowed opposition:       -- from impedance
    -- total opposition to a demand arriving at a rate, combining relational
    -- resistance with the net of invariant and constant reactance.

borrowed resonance:        -- from resonant frequency, 1 / sqrt(L * C)
    -- the rate at which invariant and accumulated will cancel, leaving only
    -- relational will to resist. An agent is LEAST protected from a demand
    -- arriving at its own resonant rate.
    -- Because the constant is the invariant's own, this rate is fixed once the
    -- invariant and the charge-constant law are fixed. That does NOT make it a
    -- discriminator; see nd-rate-discriminates.

borrowed damping:          -- from the damping ratio
    -- relational will is what damps oscillation between invariant and
    -- accumulated will. Below one the will oscillates; at one it settles
    -- fastest without overshoot; above one it is sluggish.

borrowed dissipation:      -- from resistive power, I^2 * R
    -- relational will is the ONLY dissipative term. What is spent in relation
    -- to other agents is not recoverable by the agent, while invariant and
    -- accumulated will are stored and returnable.
    -- This is a consequence of the transported FORM. It is not an ethical
    -- claim, and in particular it is not an argument for or against spending
    -- will on others.


-- =============================================================================
-- SECTION VII: GRADUATION CRITERION
-- =============================================================================

graduation:
    -- GC-1: a discriminator for the true moral operator that is not
    --       self-ascription. DISCHARGED -- d-representation-is-not-induction,
    --       with nd-rate-discriminates closing the numeric escape route.
    -- GC-2: agreement with L0 rather than a second, unrelated story.
    --       DISCHARGED -- d-self-simulation reproduces d-no-exterior.
    -- GC-3: every cross-domain bridge declared, against a fixed referent.
    --       DISCHARGED -- ax-cite-do-not-restate; four termformers, each citing
    --       a named law and quoting its form, checked against hyperphysics.
    -- GC-4: the capacitance gap resolved rather than filled by fiat.
    --       DISCHARGED by user declaration -- d-constant-will -- with the cost
    --       stated in d-transport-is-not-onto and the residue named in
    --       nd-charge-constant-law.
    -- GC-5: warrant for the electrical transport as such. NOT DISCHARGED.
    --       Tyler's own statement of it says "metaphorically analogize" and
    --       "somehow". That honesty is preserved: nothing here upgrades the
    --       analogy into a derivation, and the structural agreement noted in
    --       d-self-simulation is evidence, not warrant.
    -- GC-6: any empirical or dimensional reading of a will quantity.
    --       NOT DISCHARGED. Will has no units here.
    -- GC-7: L0's GC-5 and GC-6 -- the normative force of norm-inhabits, and
    --       the Universal Consistency Self-Maintenance Paradox.
    --       INHERITED, STILL OPEN. This layer does not touch them, and adding
    --       a will tensor does not make a descriptive structure normative.
    --
    -- Four of seven discharged. This layer does not graduate as a theory of
    -- will, and no claim of one is made anywhere in this file.
